        "event": "Winter Weather Advisory",
        "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued August 28 at 12:58PM AKDT until August 29 at 4:00PM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Snow and blowing snow. Total snow accumulations of 4 to 6\ninches at or above pass level. Wind gusts up to 30 mph. Periods of\nblowing and falling snow could reduce visibility to 1/2 mile or\nless at times. Pockets of wintry mix possible.\n\n* WHERE...Central Brooks Range, primarily Atigun Pass.\n\n* WHEN...Until 4 PM AKDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be difficult.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Snow levels have risen above 4000 feet as of\nFriday afternoon. Snow levels will fall once more towa",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Likely",
        "urgency": "Expected",
